## Contratos de integración

### ① GitHub Actions → ROP · registro del resultado de CI

**Endpoint:** `POST /v1/information-technologies/build-executions/register` (API `itmt-its-d-build-execution-management`)
**Auth:** GitHub Actions OIDC ID Token (`GitHubOIDC`) + headers estándar de Apigee (`uuid`, `ChannelId`, `sid`, `countryCode`, `businessCode`, `Idempotency-Key` = SHA-256(repositoryId:workflowRunId:runAttempt)).

| Bloque | Contenido | Quién lo consume |
|---|---|---|
| `BuildExecution` | workflowRunId, workflowRunAttempt, repository (id, fullName), commitSha, headBranch, eventName, status, conclusion, actor | ROP: decide si la versión es promovible |
| `jobs[]` → Checkout, UnitTest, Sonar, Snyk | resultados, métricas, URLs de reportes | ROP: gates de calidad y trazabilidad |
| `jobs[]` → `BuildResult` | technology, runtimeVersion, buildTool | ROP → Self Service: **technology → deploy_type** |
| `jobs[]` → `ArtifactPublishResult` | artifactName, artifactVersion, artifactRepository, artifactPath, artifactUrl, artifactDigest, packageType | **lo único que llega a AAP** |

**Lo que el ROP toma de aquí para AAP:** `repository.fullName` → `app_id` (normalizado) · `buildResult.technology` → `deploy_type` (vía Self Service) · `artifactPublishResult.{artifactName, artifactVersion, artifactUrl, artifactDigest}` · `workflowRunId` (trazabilidad).

